hadiths[34]{hadithnumber,text}:
"18280","Hushaym narrated to us, Abu Bishr informed us from Mujahid from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla from Kab ibn Ujrah, he said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at al-Hudaybiyah in pilgrim sanctity, and the idolaters had besieged us, and I had full hair so lice began falling upon my face. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by me and said: Do the lice of your head harm you. I said: Yes. So he ordered him to shave. He said: And this verse came down: But whoever among you is ill or has ailment of the head, then ransom by fasting or charity or rite."
"18281","Hushaym narrated to us, Khalid informed us from Abu Qilabah from Kab ibn Ujrah, he said: I became lousy until I thought every hair of my head had lice from its root to its tip. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered me when he saw that, saying: Shave, and the verse came down. He said: Feed six poor persons three sa of dates."
"18282","Ismail ibn Umar narrated to us, Dawud ibn Qays narrated to us from Sad ibn Ishaq ibn so-and-so ibn Kab ibn Ujrah that Abu Thumamah al-Hannat narrated to him that Kab ibn Ujrah narrated to him, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: When one of you performs ablution well then goes out heading for prayer, let him not interlock his hands, for he is in prayer."
"18283","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Sufyan informed us from al-Amash from al-Hakam from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla from Kab ibn Ujrah that a man said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): O Messenger of Allah, we know the greeting upon you, so how is prayer upon you. He said: Say: O Allah, bless Muhammad and the family of Muhammad as You blessed Ibrahim, You are Praiseworthy, Glorious. O Allah, favor Muhammad and the family of Muhammad as You favored Ibrahim, You are Praiseworthy, Glorious."
"18284","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us from Shubah, he said: al-Hakam narrated to me from Ibn Abi Layla."
"18285","He said: And Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah informed us from al-Hakam, he said: I heard Ibn Abi Layla, he said: Kab ibn Ujrah met me, Ibn Jafar said he said: Shall I not present you a gift. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to us and we said: O Messenger of Allah, we know or we recognized how is the greeting upon you, so how is prayer. He said: Say: O Allah, bless Muhammad and the family of Muhammad as You blessed the family of Ibrahim, You are Praiseworthy, Glorious. O Allah, favor Muhammad and the family of Muhammad as You favored the family of Ibrahim, You are Praiseworthy, Glorious."
"18286","He said: I read to Abd al-Rahman: Malik from Abd al-Karim ibn Malik al-Jazari from Mujahid from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla from Kab ibn Ujrah that he was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and lice in his head harmed him, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered him to shave his head and said: Fast three days, or feed six poor persons two mudds two mudds for each person, or sacrifice a sheep, whichever you do suffices you."
"18287","Ismail narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us from Mujahid from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla from Kab ibn Ujrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to me while I was kindling under a pot with lice scattering upon my face, or he said upon my eyebrows, and said: Do the lice of your head harm you. He said: I said: Yes. He said: Then shave it, and fast three days, or feed six poor persons, or sacrifice an animal. Ayyub said: I do not know with which he began."
"18288","Affan narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, al-Hakam informed me, he said: I heard Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, he said: Kab ibn Ujrah met me and mentioned the hadith."
"18289","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Asbahani from Abdullah ibn Maqil, he said: I sat with Kab ibn Ujrah while he was in the mosque and asked him about this verse: Then ransom by fasting or charity or rite. He said: So Kab said: It was revealed about me. I had ailment of my head and was carried to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with lice scattering upon my face, and he said: I did not think hardship had reached you as I see. Do you find a sheep. So I said: No. Then this verse came down: Then ransom by fasting or charity or rite. He said: Fasting three days, or feeding six poor persons half a sa of food for each poor person. He said: So it was revealed about me specially, and it is for you generally."
"18290","Affan narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Asbahani narrated to us, he said: I heard Abdullah ibn Maqil saying: I sat with Kab in this mosque and mentioned its meaning."
"18291","Bahz narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Asbahani narrated to us, he said: I heard Abdullah ibn Maqil, he said: I sat with Kab ibn Ujrah in this mosque and asked him about this verse and mentioned the hadith, and he said: Feed six poor persons each poor person half a sa of food."
"18292","Hajjaj narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhib informed us from Said al-Maqburi from a man of Banu Salim from his father from his grandfather from Kab ibn Ujrah that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No man purifies himself in his house then goes out intending only prayer but he is in prayer until he completes his prayer, and none of you should interlace his fingers in prayer."
"18293","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us from Ibn Abi Najih from Mujahid from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla from Kab ibn Ujrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw me with my lice falling upon my face and said: Do these lice of yours harm you. He said: I said: Yes. He said: So he ordered me to shave while at al-Hudaybiyah, though it had not been clarified to them that they would shave there while hoping to enter Makkah. So Allah sent down the ransom, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered me to feed a faraq among six poor persons, or fast three days, or slaughter a sheep."
"18294","Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, Muhammad ibn Ajlan informed me from Said al-Maqburi from one of the sons of Kab ibn Ujrah from Kab that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you perform ablution well then head to the mosque, you are in prayer, so do not interlock your fingers."
"18295","Qurran ibn Tamam Abu Tamam al-Asadi narrated to us from Muhammad ibn Ajlan from Said ibn Abi Said from Kab ibn Ujrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you perform ablution well then go out heading to the mosque, do not interlock your fingers. Qurran said: I think he said: For you are in prayer."
"18296","Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, Amr ibn Dinar informed me from Yahya ibn Jadah from Kab ibn Ujrah that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered Kab to shave his head because of lice. He said: Fast three days, or feed six poor persons two mudds two mudds, or slaughter."
"18297","Affan narrated to us, Wuhayb narrated to us, Khalid narrated to us from Abu Qilabah from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla from Kab ibn Ujrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to me at the time of al-Hudaybiyah while I had much hair and said: As if the lice of your head harm you. So I said: Yes. He said: Then shave it, and slaughter a sheep, or fast three days, or give charity of three sa of dates among six poor persons."
"18298","Ishaq ibn Sulayman al-Razi narrated to us, Mughirah ibn Muslim informed me from Matar al-Warraq from Ibn Sirin from Kab ibn Ujrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioned a trial and brought it near and magnified it. He said: Then a veiled man in a cloak passed, so he said: This one on that day is upon the truth. So I went hurrying, or he said hastening, and took his upper arm and said: This one, O Messenger of Allah. He said: This one, and it was Uthman ibn Affan, may Allah be pleased with him."
"18299","Muammal ibn Ismail narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Asbahani from Abdullah ibn Maqil ibn Muqarrin from Kab ibn Ujrah that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered him to fast three days, or feed six poor persons, or slaughter a sheep."
"18300","Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Sulayman that is Ibn Qarm narrated to us from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Asbahani from Abdullah ibn Maqil al-Muzani, he said: I heard Kab ibn Ujrah saying in this mosque, meaning the mosque of Kufa: About me this verse was revealed. We went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and entered pilgrim sanctity for umrah, and lice fell in my head and beard and eyebrows and mustache. That reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he sent to me and called me, and when he saw me he said: Affliction has befallen you while we did not know. Call the barber. When he came he ordered him and he shaved me. He said: Can you afford an animal. I said: No. He said: Then fast three days, or feed six poor persons, for each poor person half a sa of dates."
"18301","Affan narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, al-Hakam informed us, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Ka'b ibn Ujrah, he said: It was revealed concerning me."
"18302","Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Dawud, from al-Sha'bi, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Ka'b ibn Ujrah, this hadith."
"18303","Hushaim narrated to us, Ash'ath informed us, from al-Sha'bi, from Abdullah ibn Ma'qil, from Ka'b ibn Ujrah, similar to that, except that he said: Feed the poor three sa's of dates among six poor persons."
"18304","Ismail and Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Dawud, from al-Sha'bi, from Ka'b ibn Ujrah, Ibn Abi Adi said: Ka'b entered ihram with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he mentioned it, and they both said: Three sa's of dates among six poor persons."
"18305","Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abi Layla, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, commanded Ka'b, when he shaved his head, to slaughter a sheep, or fast three days, or feed a faraq among six poor persons."
"18306","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Sufyan, Abu Husayn narrated to me, from al-Sha'bi, from Asim al-Adawi, from Ka'b ibn Ujrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came out to us, or entered, while we were nine, and among us was a cushion of leather, and he said: There will be after me rulers who lie and commit wrong, so whoever enters upon them and believes them in their lying and helps them in their wrongdoing, he is not of me and I am not of him, and he will not come to me at the Basin, and whoever does not believe them in their lying and does not help them in their wrongdoing, he is of me and I am of him, and he will come to me at the Basin."
"18307","Abdah ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Mis'ar informed us, from al-Hakam, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Ka'b ibn Ujrah, that a man asked the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, we have learned the greeting of peace upon you, so how is the prayer for blessing, so he taught him to say: O Allah, send blessing upon Muhammad and upon the family of Muhammad as You sent blessing upon the family of Ibrahim, indeed You are Praiseworthy, Glorious, and bless Muhammad and the family of Muhammad as You blessed the family of Ibrahim, indeed You are Praiseworthy, Glorious."
"18308","Yahya narrated to us, from Sayf, he said: I heard Mujahid saying, Ibn Abi Layla narrated to me, he said: Ka'b ibn Ujrah narrated to me that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, stopped by him at al-Hudaybiyah, he said, while his head was dropping lice, he said: Do your vermin harm you, he said: I said: Yes, he said: Then shave your head, he said: Concerning me was revealed: Whoever among you is ill or has an ailment of his head, then a ransom of fasting or charity or sacrifice, he said: So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, commanded me and said: Fast three days, or give charity with a faraq among six, or a sacrifice, whatever is easy."
"18309","Yazid narrated to us, Hisham informed us, from Muhammad, from Ka'b ibn Ujrah, he said: I was with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he mentioned a trial and brought it near, then a man passed by wrapped up, and he said: This one on that day is upon guidance, he said: So I followed him until I took hold of his upper arms and turned his face toward him and uncovered his head, and I said: This one, O Messenger of Allah, he said: Yes, and behold, it was Uthman ibn Affan, may Allah be pleased with him."
"18310","Yazid narrated to us, Sharik ibn Abdullah informed us, from Muhammad ibn Ajlan, from al-Maqburi, from Ka'b ibn Ujrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came in upon me in the mosque while I had interlaced my fingers, and he said to me: O Ka'b, when you are in the mosque, do not interlace your fingers, for you are in prayer as long as you wait for the prayer."
"18311","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Mujahid, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Ka'b ibn Ujrah, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, commanded him to shave his head, or offer a sacrifice, or fast three days, or feed a faraq among six poor persons."
"18312","Hashim narrated to us, Isa ibn al-Musayyab al-Bajali narrated to us, from al-Sha'bi, from Ka'b ibn Ujrah, he said: While I was sitting in the mosque of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, leaning our backs against the qibla of the mosque of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, seven men, four of them our freedmen and three of our Arabs, when the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came out to us for the noon prayer until he reached us, and he said: What keeps you sitting here, we said: O Messenger of Allah, we are waiting for the prayer, he said: Then he fell silent a little, then he raised his head and said: Do you know what your Lord, mighty and majestic, says, we said: Allah and His Messenger know best, he said: Your Lord, mighty and majestic, says: Whoever prays the prayer at its time and guards it and does not neglect it, belittling its right, then I have a covenant upon Me to admit him to Paradise, and whoever does not pray it at its time and does not guard it and neglects it, belittling its right, then there is no covenant for him, if I will I punish him, and if I will I forgive him."
"18313","Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Ka'b, he said: When: Indeed Allah and His angels send blessing upon the Prophet, was revealed, they said: How do we send blessing upon you, O Prophet of Allah, he said: Say: O Allah, send blessing upon Muhammad and upon the family of Muhammad as You sent blessing upon Ibrahim and upon the family of Ibrahim, indeed You are Praiseworthy, Glorious, and bless Muhammad and upon the family of Muhammad as You blessed Ibrahim and upon the family of Ibrahim, indeed You are Praiseworthy, Glorious, he said: And we say: And upon us with them, Yazid said: I do not know whether it is something Ibn Abi Layla added on his own, or something Ka'b narrated."
